      "content": "That doesn't sound right. I've reviewed the official architecture documentation for our \"staged execution model,\" and there is nothing in there about delaying scan initialization until *after* the integrity gate has already passed. The documentation clearly states that the integrity gate is dependent on the completion of the Deep-Scan suite.\n\nIf the gate passed at 02:45 and the scans didn't start until 03:05, then for a 20-minute window, we were essentially running code that hadn't been validated against our security baseline. That's not a \"staged execution\"—that's a blind spot. \n\nAre you telling me that the system is designed to vouch for the integrity of modules before it has actually inspected them? I need to know if the 'PASS' was actually a bypass to ensure the 03:00 deadline was met.",
